  "coverage_93pct_explanation": "Root cause of 93.150% non-idle native coverage across longrun_3600f: Frames 0..1799 (Scenario C) correspond to attract/opening sequences where idle wait loops (0x0032E8) absorb 55.2% of total CPU cycles (9,730,133 idle vs 7,897,637 non-idle, non-idle native coverage 67.147%). In contrast, frames 1800..3599 introduce injected gameplay inputs engaging active beach combat against multiple simultaneously active enemy entities. During active combat, the game loop spends nearly 100% of CPU time executing: 1) 0x00BCBA/0x00BCD8 hitbox bounding-box queries across all active entity pairs; 2) 0x015AE2 physics displacement and velocity integration for player and enemies; 3) 0x02ED20 3D screen coordinate projection and viewport culling; 4) Production helpers 0x008E90 (tilemap/scroll update), 0x00A7E6, 0x00A342, 0x00B34C, and 0x008E22. Because virtually all heavy arithmetic and per-entity loops are compiled (196 production helpers + M15.245 + M15.246), idle loop waiting drops to 0% in frames 3000..3600 (Windows 10 & 11), concentrating CPU time inside already-native routines and elevating overall non-idle native coverage to 93.150%.",
